{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "07", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "57", "S": "26"}}, "news": [{"title": "Jharkhand government targets one lakh new PMAY-Urban houses approval this year", "para": "Jharkhand aims for one lakh new Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Urban houses this year.  Urban local bodies will invite fresh applications from eligible families.  Construction of nearly fourteen thousand houses will reach roof level soon.  Funds are available, and beneficiaries' payments must be expedited.  Banks will receive more home loan applications for affordable housing projects.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/jharkhand-government-targets-one-lakh-new-pmay-urban-houses-approval-this-year/133025119?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-43758/133025119.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "No immediate relief for Ram Charan, Chamundi in Boulder Hills plots case", "para": "Actor Ram Charan and former cricketer Chamundeswaranath faced a setback as their plea for villa plots was turned down. The SAFEMA Appellate Tribunal is set to review their claims as bona fide purchasers. These premium plots, totaling more than fourteen crore rupees, require buyers to validate their transactions with legitimate funds. The special court is scheduled to examine their case and presented evidence.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/no-immediate-relief-for-ram-charan-chamundi-in-boulder-hills-plots-case/133020006?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-241018/133020006.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "SC pulls up banks over alleged nexus with builders in real estate cases", "para": "In a significant ruling, the Supreme Court has ordered lenders to proceed with prosecuting their officers implicated in a questionable alliance with builders. The court's directive includes the allocation of extra police forces to bolster the CBI's ongoing probe. Additionally, pertinent case details will be handed over to the Enforcement Directorate, as the CBI scrutinizes allegations tied to certain real estate firms.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/sc-pulls-up-banks-over-alleged-nexus-with-builders-in-real-estate-cases/133019734?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-97496/133019734.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}